{"change_summary":"No tracked-file fixes were required in the main repo for this apply-fixes pass. I audited the approved reproduction and habitat-probe deliverable against the final review, confirmed the remaining note about warm-side temperature curve constants is a documented low-priority tuning follow-up rather than a blocking defect, and revalidated the current tree without changing project code.","outstanding_risks":["I did not rerun the full workspace, full `tank_core` suite, or `cargo clippy`; validation was limited to formatting plus the targeted reproduction and habitat-geometry regression binaries.","The working tree still contains unrelated infrastructure dirtiness outside this deliverable (`.claude/worktrees/tanksim-6e5.4.7` and untracked `.ralph-burning/`), which I left untouched."],"steps":[{"description":"Reviewed the final approved review output and the current tree to determine whether any blocking follow-up fixes still remained for the reproduction deliverable.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Inspected the reproduction parameter surfaces and habitat-probe assertions referenced by the review; skipped tracked-file edits because the remaining note was a non-blocking future tunability suggestion and the current implementation already satisfies the accepted criteria.","order":2,"status":"skipped"},{"description":"Ran targeted formatting and regression validation on the current tree to confirm the approved reproduction and habitat-probe behavior remains green.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["Source audit confirmed `reproductive_readiness_smoothing` remains species/runtime-backed, while `LOW_TEMP_REPRO_MIN_FACTOR`, `HIGH_TEMP_REPRO_SHOULDER_FACTOR`, and `MIN_REPRO_SUPPRESSION_FACTOR` remain documented fixed file-level constants in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs`, matching the final review's non-blocking note.","`cargo fmt --all --check` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors -- --nocapture` passed with 16/16 tests.","`cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_habitat_geometry_probes -- --nocapture` passed; `all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary` still reports `Probe 4: substrate_redox [PASS]` with suboxic volume `5055->5746 / 191->0 cm³`.","`git status --short` and `git diff --name-only HEAD --` show no tracked project-file delta from this pass; only the pre-existing `.claude/worktrees/tanksim-6e5.4.7` dirtiness and untracked `.ralph-burning/` remain."]}